    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/moenkhausia_sanctaefilomenae_wild_en/",
      "html": "<p>Some fish species are so common in the trade that we sometimes forget to look at them with the eyes of a child. One of these is the red eye tetra, one of the top classics among ornamental fish. It can be found in any pet shop around the world. Usually these fish in the trade are tank-reared, but here wild-collected specimens from Paraguay were obtained.</p><p>Etymology: Moenkhausia is a dedication name for W. J. Moenkhaus, a friend of Eigenmann, the describer of the genus. sanctaefilomenae refers to the collection site of the type specimens (\"lagoon near St. Filomena at the Parnahyba\").</p>"
    }
  ],
